<title>INDIA: India soybean prices steady on equal demand,supply.</title>
<headline>India soybean prices steady on equal demand,supply.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady in central Indian markets on Thursday on equal demand and supply, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soyoil solvent was down by 100 rupees per tonne on increased selling while demand from refineries and vanaspati units was limited. Soyoil refined was steady and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices were firm on firm overseas trends. Soymeal yellow was $283-284 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $122 per tonne for ready shipment and was $115 per tonne for March-April shipment. Rapeseed extraction was 4,250 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,200 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
